# Plot Theme

Use this **modern dark theme** for all matplotlib plots (notebook and scripts).

- **Style:** `plt.style.use('dark_background')`
- **Background:** Figure and axes `facecolor='#1a1a1a'`
- **Lines:** Distinct colors (e.g. `#00d4aa`, `#7b68ee`), `linewidth=2`
- **Text:** Title `color='#e0e0e0'`, axis labels/ticks `color='#b0b0b0'`
- **Grid:** `ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3, color='#404040')`
- **Spines:** `ax.spines[:].set_color('#404040')`
- **Legend:** `ax.legend(framealpha=0.2)`

Example:

```python
plt.style.use('dark_background')
fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 6), facecolor='#1a1a1a')
ax.set_facecolor('#1a1a1a')
ax.plot(x, y, color='#00d4aa', linewidth=2)
ax.set_title('Title', fontsize=14, color='#e0e0e0')
ax.set_xlabel('X', color='#b0b0b0')
ax.set_ylabel('Y', color='#b0b0b0')
ax.tick_params(colors='#b0b0b0')
ax.legend(framealpha=0.2)
ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3, color='#404040')
ax.spines[:].set_color('#404040')
```
